{"name":"Great Coat Grey","hex":"#7f8488","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"great","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Taking up a lot of space; large.\n\n Much, more than usual.","Much, more than usual."]},{"part":"Interjection","definitions":["Expression of gladness and content about something.","A sarcastic inversion thereof."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/great"},{"term":"coat","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An outer garment covering the upper torso and arms.","A covering of material, such as paint."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To cover with a coating of some material.","To cover like a coat."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/coat"},{"term":"grey","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Commonwealth standard spelling of gray.","Synonym of coloured (pertaining to the mixed race of black and white)."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["Commonwealth standard spelling of gray."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/grey"}],"entries":[{"title":"Greatcoat","blocks":[{"text":"A greatcoat, a large, woollen overcoat designed for warmth and for protection against wind and weather, features a collar that can be turned up and cuffs that can be turned down to protect the face and the hands, while the short rain-cape at the shoulders protects from the wind and repels rain. In the 19th century, such a coat was part of a soldier's military uniform, to be worn while on watch, hence the term watchcoat."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/51/Grande_Arm%C3%A9e_-_Light_Infantry_Officers_in_Greatcoats.jpg/330px-Grande_Arm%C3%A9e_-_Light_Infantry_Officers_in_Greatcoats.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Greatcoat","wikidata":"Q422821"},{"title":"Coat","blocks":[{"text":"A coat is an outer garment for the upper body, worn by any gender for warmth or fashion. Coats typically have long sleeves and are open down the front, and closing by means of buttons, zippers, hook-and-loop fasteners, toggles, a belt, or a combination of some of these. Other possible features include collars, shoulder straps, and hoods."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8e/FalatJulian.PortretAntoniegoWodzickiego.1900.ws.jpg/330px-FalatJulian.PortretAntoniegoWodzickiego.1900.ws.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Coat","wikidata":"Q152574"},{"title":"Grey","blocks":[{"text":"Grey or gray is an intermediate color between black and white. It is a neutral or achromatic color, meaning that it has no chroma. It is the color of a rain or storm cloud, of ash, and of lead."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1e/Loxodonta_africana_by_Ron_Cogswell.jpg/330px-Loxodonta_africana_by_Ron_Cogswell.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Grey","wikidata":"Q42519"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3b/French_cavalry_man%27s_cloak_from_1812.JPG/120px-French_cavalry_man%27s_cloak_from_1812.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3b/French_cavalry_man%27s_cloak_from_1812.JPG/250px-French_cavalry_man%27s_cloak_from_1812.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3b/French_cavalry_man%27s_cloak_from_1812.JPG/120px-French_cavalry_man%27s_cloak_from_1812.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AFrench_cavalry_man's_cloak_from_1812.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/79/Soldier_in_greatcoat_%283774187%29.jpg/120px-Soldier_in_greatcoat_%28377